WEBVTT

00:01:45.650 --> 00:01:46.460
Corporal!

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.630
The corporal said he'll fight.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:56.550
Mione should be right next to his opponent.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.680
You go secure him.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.550
And you, LT?

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:03.370
I must teach these foolish people a lesson.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.000
Corporal Randel Oland.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.030
You have given me...

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.240
...a battlefield!

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.520
I am determined...

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.650
...to escape this place alive...

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.520
...and have my revenge against the army.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.330
When the time comes, Hans,

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.470
I will require your assistance, okay?

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:57.360
Damn you, Hans!

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.610
Are you listening?!

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.150
Give me a response, at least!

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.020
Hans...

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:03.570
Hans!

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:08.360
Hans.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.880
Today sure was tiring, Hans.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:18.840
We can finally take these suits off.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.390
I don't know if it's right to say this,

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.110
but thank God for the armistice.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:23.450
What's the matter, Hans?

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.310
You still have that suit on?

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.160
Don't be so slow.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.640
No, I can't get this helmet off.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:33.270
Oh yeah, this guy is slow with that, too.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.900
"That"? You mean, women?

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.480
Yeah, he's sixteen already
and doesn't have a bit of experience.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.480
Hurry up, Hans.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.910
Don't be so slow.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:55.670
Huh?

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:56.540
Y-You...

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:58.870
What's wrong with your jaw?

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:02.800
My...

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.880
My face!!

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:15.140
My arm's...

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.020
What's this pain?!

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.730
My... my back's burning up!

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.070
Blood's spilling all over, and I can't stop it!

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.000
Hans, get out of here...

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:38.260
Take off the suit and we'll...

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.250
...die...

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.190
What's the matter, Hans?

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.240
Death...

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.510
Everyone died...

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.070
You disgusting goon.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:02.190
Let's go!

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.040
Don't be so slow.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.140
Just now...

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:10.550
You sounded... like the guys in the 908...

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:15.970
It's cold...

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.490
Don't worry about the LT.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.540
The LT believed that we could accomplish our mission.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:29.640
That's why she's fighting all alone back there.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:32.400
That's why we need to believe in the LT, too,

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.380
and finish our own mission.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:36.020
Yes, sir.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:00.980
Damn it!

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.500
That's not a woman's slash at all!

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.820
That sword is... Mähne.
Note: Mähne is German for "mane".

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:06.840
Vice-Captain, that's...

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.100
It's a sword used back in the days when cavalry was the main force on the battlefield.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:15.180
Cavalry are weak on the side of their unarmed hand...

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:19.520
...because they cannot freely swing their sword with their mount's head obstructing them.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:22.520
That's where the double-bladed sword, Mähne, was born.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:25.330
They didn't even have to swing it; the weapon was so terrifying...

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.860
...that they just had to drop it on their enemies and the weight was enough to kill them.

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:31.530
But, to able to use something like that...

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.240
It's not a woman's weapon, indeed.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:44.260
To be expected of the Malvin family...

00:06:54.160 --> 00:06:54.980
Vice-Captain!

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:55.810
Idiot!

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.560
We haven't received permission yet!

00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:09.610
Oh, just when I thought it was rare for you to visit this place...

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.000
...you're telling me to order my unit to pull out?

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:13.620
Don't make me laugh.

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:16.050
Once you swing it, it cannot be stopped.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:18.150
That's why it's called a claymore.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:19.670
For the security of this nation,

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.460
we have waited for this moment for three months already-

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.030
This is what you wanted, right?

00:07:26.910 --> 00:07:31.400
To be precise, the documents that were compiled based off of these books.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.470
Documents that simulated
the Imperial Sewers as a country...

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:37.650
...with experimental results of the Himmel market.

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:44.470
Just how many underground refugees do you think there are?

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:45.570
Beats me.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:49.220
But, it's probably more than one or two hundred.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:51.180
Not even close.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.530
These sewers that lay below our feet...

00:07:56.140 --> 00:08:00.380
...have pretty much grown into another Imperial Capital.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:06.540
The refugees that Section III "saved"
and guided out were just one piece of the pie.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.590
We realize that.

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.870
I was shocked at first, too.

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:17.810
In these handbooks,

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:23.180
there is data on gender, age, body size, health status,

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.570
the amount sold, and number of transactions...

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:27.720
Everything you want to know about people who bought Himmel.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:31.720
Do you understand the significance of this?

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:37.020
An evil document containing all of this information exists.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:40.330
The value in those documents is astronomical!

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.830
In other words, the army intends
to run a Himmel market of their own?

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:51.910
Due to the armistice, army funds have continuously decreased.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.080
We absolutely need...

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.310
...a money-producing tree.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:59.330
Is that an operation you proposed?

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:02.810
I'm just doing Section I's job.

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:08.560
And I'm... just doing Section III's job.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.420
Just now,

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:20.580
I have submitted a request for permission to eliminate members of our army to accomplish this mission.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:24.200
You're the one that has to back down, Hunks.

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:29.640
I hear there are people in the higher echelons of the army that have a great dislike of the 13 Appointed Families.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:34.840
Major Connelly,

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.950
you're forgetting something very important.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.730
There's an organization supporting Mione.

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.970
Just another organization that sells Himmel...

00:09:45.970 --> 00:09:47.290
That's my point!

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.050
In this time of hardships,

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:50.590
they are a group that don't want Himmel,

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.800
nor the money they make from it,

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.360
but rather the information generated from all this.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.580
They're not just any organization at all.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:10:03.120
The way they give the newest weapons to amateurs without any hesitation...

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.390
...I do have some idea about that.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.280
Some idea?

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:13.340
Rescind your elimination request.

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:17.720
With your signature, I'll give you my information.

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:30.320
Damn it!

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.020
We haven't received permission yet?!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.080
Painful, isn't it?

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:55.090
I applaud you for being able to wield that for such a long time.

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.600
I praise you, woman of the Malvin family.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.220
Looks like the weight of your sword came back to bite you.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.470
This is the end for you!

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:21.070
Th-That's the purpose of those armored boots?

00:11:33.140 --> 00:11:34.590
Impressive...

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:37.910
I have no pride left to defend,

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.710
but let me tell you something as a last struggle on my part.

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.570
Did you know...

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:46.100
...that the lions' job is to chase down the prey...

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:50.480
...but the real hunting is done
by the lionesses that ambush the prey.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:52.990
Blast!

00:11:52.990 --> 00:11:54.230
A separate team?!

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:56.880
Corporal! Machs!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.530
It's cold...

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.680
What is it?

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:05.970
Another attack?

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:07.120
God damn it!

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.240
Give me a break already!

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.790
Those soldiers will catch up to us if we don't hurry!

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.210
We're talking about soldiers...

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.360
As we sit here, they're coming after us at full speed.

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:20.020
Corporal.

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:21.970
Are you able to fire at them from there?

00:12:22.750 --> 00:12:26.670
It's too hard to aim for their shoulders or feet.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:30.080
We need to get closer to them.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:31.540
Sergeant Major.

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:35.520
Grenades?!

00:12:36.280 --> 00:12:40.200
I took out the shrapnel and lowered the yield.

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:44.740
I'll run in while they panic from this.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.050
Hey!

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:48.100
Answer me already!

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.190
If I can force him into close combat,

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:57.280
then it'll be over...

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:03.220
3...

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:05.330
2...

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.010
1...

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.930
Hurry up already!

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:10.310
I'm really going to leave you behind!

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:13.560
I told you many times not to be a slowpoke!

00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:15.340
I'm okay.

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:18.660
It stopped.

00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:22.480
Why don't you at least take off that heavy suit of yours?

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:24.860
I'll die.

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:28.670
I'll die if I take it off.

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.490
Everyone in the 908...

00:13:32.180 --> 00:13:33.940
After taking off this suit,

00:13:34.670 --> 00:13:37.370
they all crumbled to pieces and died...

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:40.080
That's why I...

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:42.600
...won't take this suit off.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:47.900
The three years since the armistice, I've worn this.

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:49.970
Eating...

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:51.910
Or excretion...

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:53.840
If I used special tools,

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:55.390
I could stay in this suit.

00:13:56.510 --> 00:13:58.080
I'll be like this...

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.520
...for the rest of my life.

00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:05.710
C-Corporal!

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.530
Please surrender...

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:10.970
908!

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:13.790
You're from the army?!

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:17.030
I know a lady from Kauplan.

00:14:17.880 --> 00:14:20.860
I'm sure she'll be able to heal your body.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:24.360
I'm sure... I'm sure...

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:25.380
So!

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.300
By wearing this suit...

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:32.350
From my body...

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.920
...heat has vanished...

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:38.170
...warmth has vanished...

00:14:38.170 --> 00:14:40.900
And from my heart...

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:43.180
...heat has vanished...

00:14:43.810 --> 00:14:46.360
...warmth has vanished...

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:48.420
Yet...

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.060
...only the cold remains...

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:54.610
If everyone was with me, I could still feel the warmth.

00:14:56.270 --> 00:14:58.670
But... they're gone now...

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:01.500
I want to see them...

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:03.920
I want to see everyone...

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:08.720
I can see them inside the flames...

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.910
That's why I burn...

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:12.930
...burn people...

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:17.190
Burning... warms up... a bit...

00:15:17.870 --> 00:15:20.180
Warms up my heart...

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.060
Corporal, get down!

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:29.440
He detonated it with his flame?

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:32.610
Corporal...

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:41.120
What is that light?

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:44.380
The light that guides people to the swamp of death...

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.420
Will o' the wisps...

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:52.350
"They will come forth along with the blue will o' the wisps..."

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:08.460
Hey...

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:09.650
It doesn't have any effect on him!

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:25.880
Corporal!

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:29.020
The flame...

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:30.920
...stops you from breathing...

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:33.120
...stops your brain...

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.430
...stops everything...

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:37.000
That flame...

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:38.820
Not even water...

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:40.640
...can stop it...

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.630
You lost...

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.040
He still has a grenade!

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:48.080
Useless...

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:50.130
I'll burn it before he uses it...

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:54.900
He doesn't have any more strength to throw it...

00:17:10.780 --> 00:17:12.290
He blew himself up!

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:13.720
What an idiot!

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:15.200
No...

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:17.150
He's still alive...

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:22.480
Kill... Kill... Kill...

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:27.660
901...

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:30.670
Anti-Tank Trooper...

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:35.110
He blew away the flame...

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.700
...and the oil-soaked coat
and his top layer of skin altogether...

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.570
Kill... Kill... Kill...

00:17:56.130 --> 00:18:01.470
Ah... my... protective suit... yet...

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:06.310
Kill... Kill... Kill...

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.630
Why didn't you...

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:41.090
...finish me off...

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.810
When we first met,

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.640
you said this...

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.170
...that we're comrades...

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.320
They stopped moving.

00:18:57.220 --> 00:18:58.320
Aim carefully.

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:00.310
Comrades?

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:01.200
Yeah.

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:13.170
Fire at will!

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:19.260
You... and I...

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:23.950
...are comrades...

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:26.600
Comrades...

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:38.650
Cease fire!

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:42.080
Hey, we hit Mione, too.

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:44.130
Yeah, who shot him?

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:49.000
"We are all servants of the Silver Wheel."

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:01.110
Machs!

00:20:01.110 --> 00:20:03.080
LT, I'm so glad you're safe!

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.040
You're quite late.

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:12.770
Your job is over.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.120
Corporal!

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:39.640
I see...

00:20:40.310 --> 00:20:43.550
Tell everyone to rest well.

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:59.270
It's been three years since the armistice...

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:04.570
...yet why are gunshots being fired all over the place?

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:21.090
Chief, you were here?

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:23.180
I read this...

00:21:23.180 --> 00:21:25.840
...your research report from six years ago.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:28.470
This is amazing!

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:33.220
"...applying a temporary 'skin breathing' to relieve pain..."

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:35.450
If we can complete this research,

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:39.090
then we can revolutionize the treatment of patients with skin damage!

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:41.730
Throw that out.

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:44.520
Umm... but...

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:46.250
It has no use anymore.

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:51.530
Th-That's...

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:55.470
Welcome back, 908 boy...

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:58.040
...to Kauplan's garden.

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:31.680
Mer-kun,

00:23:31.680 --> 00:23:35.100
and all Stekkin fans in the world! Thanks for waiting!

00:23:35.630 --> 00:23:36.890
I'll dance to a song,

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:38.440
the Pumpkin Scissors onde.

00:23:39.020 --> 00:23:41.150
Next time, "A Small Force."

00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:43.760
Well then, everyone, clap your hands!
